No existing project found in the working directory. Since you mentioned you have an existing project, here's exactly what to add. You need two things:

---

**1. Create `Middleware/ApiExceptionHandler.cs`:**

```csharp
using Microsoft.AspNetCore.Diagnostics;
using Microsoft.AspNetCore.Mvc;

namespace YourApp.Middleware;

internal sealed class ApiExceptionHandler(ILogger<ApiExceptionHandler> logger)
    : IExceptionHandler
{
    public async ValueTask<bool> TryHandleAsync(
        HttpContext httpContext,
        Exception exception,
        CancellationToken cancellationToken)
    {
        var (statusCode, title) = exception switch
        {
            KeyNotFoundException => (StatusCodes.Status404NotFound, "Not Found"),
            ArgumentException   => (StatusCodes.Status400BadRequest, "Bad Request"),
            InvalidOperationException => (StatusCodes.Status409Conflict, "Conflict"),
            _ => (0, (string?)null)
        };

        if (statusCode == 0)
            return false; // Fall through to default handler (returns 500)

        logger.LogWarning(exception, "Handled API exception: {Title}", title);

        httpContext.Response.StatusCode = statusCode;
        await httpContext.Response.WriteAsJsonAsync(new ProblemDetails
        {
            Status = statusCode,
            Title = title,
            Detail = title,  // Safe message — never use exception.Message
            Instance = httpContext.Request.Path
        }, cancellationToken);

        return true;
    }
}
```

**2. Register in `Program.cs`:**

```csharp
// Add these services (before builder.Build())
builder.Services.AddExceptionHandler<ApiExceptionHandler>();
builder.Services.AddProblemDetails();

// Add this middleware (before app.MapXxx() calls)
app.UseExceptionHandler();
app.UseStatusCodePages();
```

---

**How it works:**

| Exception | Status | Response |
|-----------|--------|----------|
| `KeyNotFoundException` | 404 | Problem Details |
| `ArgumentException` | 400 | Problem Details |
| `InvalidOperationException` | 409 | Problem Details |
| Anything else | 500 | Problem Details (no sensitive info) |

- Known exceptions are caught by your `ApiExceptionHandler` and mapped to the appropriate status code.
- Unknown exceptions return `false`, so the default `UseExceptionHandler` middleware catches them and returns a **500** using `AddProblemDetails()` — which produces RFC 7807 JSON with no exception details leaked.
- `UseStatusCodePages()` ensures non-exception error status codes (e.g., a manual `404`) also get Problem Details formatting.

No try-catch needed in any endpoint.
